# Netlify redirect rules — read at deploy time, ignored by Live Server.
#
# Every link in this site points at the real filename (contact.html) so that
# VS Code Live Server, which cannot resolve extensionless URLs, keeps working
# locally. These rules strip the .html once the site is on Netlify, so the
# address bar shows /contact instead of /contact.html.
#
# The trailing "!" forces the redirect. Without it Netlify would notice that
# contact.html actually exists, serve the file, and skip the rule entirely.
#
# Format: <from>  <to>  <status>

/index.html          /                301!
/about.html          /about           301!
/projects.html       /projects        301!
/contact.html        /contact         301!
/bikeshack.html      /bikeshack       301!
/squatchgolf.html    /squatchgolf     301!
/thegameofwash.html  /thegameofwash   301!
/josephmuller.html   /josephmuller    301!
